WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:08.164
Deleted something by mistake? Tickets and docs go to the trash first, so you can bring them back. In this video, you’ll restore them.

2
00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:15.079
Say this restock ticket was logged twice. Open its menu in the list, and choose Move to trash.

3
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:21.165
Worklynq checks first, and reminds you it can be restored. Confirm, and it’s gone from the list.

4
00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:29.805
In the Admin console, open Tickets trash, under Work Configuration. It lists every deleted ticket, who deleted it, and when.

5
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:36.283
To bring one back, open its menu and choose Restore. It goes back to its work area, as it was.

6
00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:44.669
You can also delete tickets for good: one at a time from the menu, or tick several and click Delete permanently. That can’t be undone.

7
00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:52.357
Pages and folders from Spaces go to Docs trash. Recover a folder, and the pages inside it come back with it.

8
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.325
Nothing is removed from the trash on its own. It stays there until someone deletes it for good.

9
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:07.913
That’s the trash, and the end of the Admin console series. You’ll find every guide, and every video, at worklynq.com/docs.

